==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|eavesdrop|ing|id2=gerund noun}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{verbal noun of|en|eavesdrop}}:
## [[listen#Verb|Listening]] [[secretly]] to the [[private#Adjective|private]] [[conversation]]s of others.
##* {{quote-book|en|author=Lawrence R. Bourne|chapter=7|title=Well Tackled!|year=1928|ol=5387037W|passage=The detective kept them in view. He made his way casually along the inside of the shelter until he reached an open scuttle close to where the two men were standing talking. '''Eavesdropping''' was not a thing Larard would have practised from choice, but there were times when, in the public interest, he had to do it, and this was one of them.}}
## {{lb|en|telecommunication}} The [[interception]] of [[electronic]] [[communication]].
## {{lb|en|zoology}} The [[act#Noun|act]] of one [[organism]] listening for another's [[call#Noun|calls]], so as to [[exploit#Verb|exploit]] them.

